Article 8 A franchisor shall, within 15 days from the date of first concluding a franchise contract, file a record with the commerce administration department in accordance with these Regulations. Where engaging in franchise activities within the scope of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government, the franchisor shall file a record with the commerce administration department of the people's government of that province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government; where engaging in franchise activities across provinces, autonomous regions, or municipalities directly under the Central Government, the franchisor shall file a record with the commerce administration department of the State Council.
To file a record with the commerce administration department, the franchisor shall submit the following documents and materials:
(1) a copy of the business license or a copy of the enterprise registration (incorporation) certificate;
(2) a sample franchise contract;
(3) the franchise operation manual;
(4) a market plan;
(5) a written commitment and relevant supporting materials demonstrating compliance with Article 7 of these Regulations;
(6) other documents and materials as prescribed by the commerce administration department of the State Council.
If the franchised products or services require approval for operation according to law, the franchisor shall also submit the relevant approval documents.

Article 11 When engaging in franchise activities, the franchisor and the franchisee shall conclude a franchise contract in writing.
A franchise contract shall include the following main contents:
(1) the basic information of the franchisor and the franchisee;
(2) the content and term of the franchise;
(3) the types, amounts, and payment methods of franchise fees;
(4) the specific content and provision methods of services such as business guidance, technical support, and business training;
(5) the quality, standard requirements, and assurance measures of products or services;
(6) the promotion and advertising of products or services;
(7) the protection of consumer rights and interests in the franchise and the bearing of compensation liability;
(8) the modification, dissolution, and termination of the franchise contract;
(9) liability for breach of contract;
(10) the methods for dispute resolution;
(11) other matters agreed upon by the franchisor and the franchisee.

Article 22 A franchisor shall provide the following information to the franchisee:
(1) the name, domicile, legal representative, registered capital amount, business scope and basic information on the franchisor's franchise activities;
(2) basic information on the franchisor's registered trademark, enterprise logo, patent, know-how and business model;
(3) the types, amounts and payment methods of franchise fees (including whether a deposit is collected and the conditions and methods for refund of the deposit);
(4) the prices and conditions for providing products, services and equipment to the franchisee;
(5) the specific contents, methods of provision and implementation plan of services such as continuous operational guidance, technical support and business training to the franchisee;
(6) the specific methods for guiding and supervising the franchisee's business activities;
(7) the investment budget for the franchise outlet;
(8) the number, geographical distribution and business condition assessment of existing franchisees within the territory of China;
(9) the summary of financial accounting reports and audit reports audited by an accounting firm for the most recent two years;
(10) the litigation and arbitration cases related to the franchise in the most recent five years;
(11) whether the franchisor and its legal representative have any records of major illegal business operations; and
(12) other information prescribed by the competent department of commerce under the State Council.
